-- title:
--   A point outside an integral projection is separated by an integer affine inequality valid on the entire projection.
-- statement:
--   A point outside an integral projection is separated by an integer affine inequality
--   valid on the entire projection. Its height depends on the number of eliminated variables
--   and the row heights, and is independent of the number of rows.
--
--   This lemma is part of OpenAI's machine-checked proof that rational linear programs can be solved by a strongly polynomial algorithm on a real-number RAM (Smale's ninth problem). It is used in the proof of `OAI.Optimization.LinearProgramming.Compression.preserves_generator_fiber`.
